issue_context.body:
Hi all,

I'm trying to use the low-level primitives (EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex) in OpenSSL to create a PSS signature. However, I get a segmentation fault from OpenSSL. I'm not sure if I'm doing something wrong, or if this is a bug (as such, I made this a question).
The following code reproduces the error:
```
#include <openssl/core_names.h>
#include <openssl/evp.h>
#include <openssl/param_build.h>
#include <openssl/params.h>
#include <openssl/rsa.h>

EVP_PKEY* generateKey() {
  EVP_PKEY*     pkey = NULL;
  EVP_PKEY_CTX* ctx  = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id(EVP_PKEY_RSA, NULL);
  EVP_PKEY_keygen_init(ctx);
  EVP_PKEY_generate(ctx, &pkey);
  assert(pkey);
  return pkey;
}

OSSL_PARAM* generateSignParams() {
  OSSL_PARAM_BLD* bld = OSSL_PARAM_BLD_new();
  OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_int(bld, OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PAD_MODE, RSA_PKCS1_PSS_PADDING);
  // This does not seem to have any effect:
  // OSSL_PARAM_BLD_push_utf8_string(bld, OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST, "sha1", 4);

  OSSL_PARAM* result = OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param(bld);
  assert(result);
  return result;
}

int main() {
  EVP_PKEY*     key = generateKey();
  EVP_PKEY_CTX* ctx = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey(NULL, key, NULL);

  // This does not seem to have any effect:
  // EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_signature_md(ctx, EVP_sha1());

  EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex(ctx, generateSignParams());  // <----------- crash in this line
}
```

This crashes within `EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex`. The stack trace at the point of the crash is as follows:
```
test.exe!EVP_MD_is_a(const evp_md_st * md, const char * name) Line 716
test.exe!rsa_check_padding(const PROV_RSA_CTX * prsactx, const char * mdname, const char * mgf1_mdname, int mdnid) Line 143
test.exe!rsa_setup_md(PROV_RSA_CTX * ctx, const char * mdname, const char * mdprops) Line 297
test.exe!rsa_set_ctx_params(void * vprsactx, const ossl_param_st * params) Line 1350
test.exe!rsa_signverify_init(void * vprsactx, void * vrsa, const ossl_param_st * params, int operation) Line 404
test.exe!rsa_sign_init(void * vprsactx, void * vrsa, const ossl_param_st * params) Line 504
test.exe!evp_pkey_signature_init(evp_pkey_ctx_st * ctx, int operation, const ossl_param_st * params) Line 473
test.exe!EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex(evp_pkey_ctx_st * ctx, const ossl_param_st * params) Line 563
```

The `md` parameter to `EVP_MD_is_a` is `NULL` (which is not allowed). This value is retrieved from `prsactx->md`, in the following code (`rsa_check_padding`):
```
                if ((mdname != NULL && !EVP_MD_is_a(prsactx->md, mdname))
                    || (mgf1_mdname != NULL
                        && !EVP_MD_is_a(prsactx->mgf1_md, mgf1_mdname))) {
```
Here, `mdname` is not `NULL`, as it was given a default value in `rsa_set_ctx_params`, due to the following code:
```
    if (prsactx->md == NULL && pmdname == NULL
        && pad_mode == RSA_PKCS1_PSS_PADDING)
        pmdname = RSA_DEFAULT_DIGEST_NAME;
```

So I can understand the crash, but I'm not sure how to fix it. Setting the message digest (as commented in my reproduction code) does not seem to have any effect.

Am I doing something wrong here, or is this a bug? How can I get this to work?

I know that there may be higher level primitives that are more suitable for this specific scenario, but we will sometimes need lower level primitives, so it would be confusing if that doesn't always work as expected.

Thanks in advance!

Best regards,
SpoofedEx
